{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project","id":1508759,"title":"Night Horrors: Scourging Thorns An fan project","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-18T09:10:05-07:00","id":1508759,"title":"Night Horrors: Scourging Thorns An fan project","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:26px\"><span style=\"color:#4e5f70\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Night Horrors: Scourging Thorns</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">An fan project</span></span></div> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Pain, it drives one mad. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">For many changelings it drives them both mad and to seek out others, however, either due to not getting that support or said support being inadagqutie to their conditions, causing them to lash out, to become ensnared in old lies, to fallow new ones, or burn down everything in order to destroy it. And even then, pain can be rarely escaped, Hobs wander the streets and their dreams are fully nightmares...</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Scourging Thorns is a Night Horrors book in which we provide a library of</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> interesting antagonists and supporting characters for anyone\u2019s</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> chronicle, whether to populate a cast or inspire compelling</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">plots tied into the tales of Changeling the lost.</span></span><br /> <br /> Goals<br /> -Flesh out The Loyalist factions of the changelings, giving them new abilities, and movitves<br /> -Give some more threats out of the hedge<br /> -NPCS<br /> <br /> <br /> Chapters<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fiction </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Introduction</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chapter 1 Privateers and their payments </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-talk about how they happen </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Gives out some sample super tokens they have </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-gives some sample NPCs </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chapter 2 The Bridger Burner and His Marvelous skill</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Talk about how they form </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Give Special merits,and how to make more of those merits </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-NPCS Chapter </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">3 the secret loyalist </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Talk about how they come to be<br /> -Give new Mantles and Contracts<br /> -NPCS Chapter<br /> <br /> 4 Spirits of Dream<br /> <br /> -Dream Enemies and enties<br /> -Bit of Beast Crossover<br /> -NPCS </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chapter 5 Out of the Hedge </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Talk about how Hobgoblins interact outside of the hedge </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-Give some new Dread powers </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Give little short exerts on how Core book Hobs interact with the Mortal</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">_hunter side bar_</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">-NPCS</span></span>\u200b<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#16a085\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">How to Join\u200b</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Start writing, I'll just sort everything later...</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Document</span></span><br /> \u200b<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1FuOtqm5TIEHICE8vz6iI5Q49lJw2zmfhH1EHDCc2xfo/edit\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...EHDCc2xfo/edit</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T10:51:24-07:00","id":1508766,"title":"","content":"This sounds wonderful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T13:47:13-07:00","id":1508773,"title":"","content":"Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T13:50:33-07:00","id":1508774,"title":"","content":"Wow! This is cool! Mind if I help work on it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T14:06:21-07:00","id":1508776,"title":"","content":"Yep, if you something you want to add, just add it, we can talk after","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T19:37:54-07:00","id":1508810,"title":"","content":"Fascinating. Chapters 4 and 5 look especially promising.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T20:12:09-07:00","id":1508813,"title":"","content":"Hey, so I\u2019ve thinking about what would happen to a Beast who enters a Bastion\u2026like a lot. Should I try and see what Beast Oneiromancy looks like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T20:21:08-07:00","id":1508815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508813#post1508813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, so I\u2019ve thinking about what would happen to a Beast who enters a Bastion\u2026like a lot. Should I try and see what Beast Oneiromancy looks like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which reminds me; by default, the dreams of the Dreaming Roads are \u2018real\u2019 dreams and not the metaphoric \u2018dreams\u2019 of the Astral/ ___<br /> Dream proper, so mundane Beasts shouldn\u2019t have much to do with fae oneiromancy.<br /> <br /> <br /> The operative words here being \u2018by default\u2019 and \u2018mundane\u2019, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T20:23:43-07:00","id":1508817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508813#post1508813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, so I\u2019ve thinking about what would happen to a Beast who enters a Bastion\u2026like a lot. Should I try and see what Beast Oneiromancy looks like?</div> </div> </div> </div>It looks like Lair Imposition and Primordial Pathways. A Beast in a Bastion is like a changeling physically being in a Bastion, except that Beasts aren't kitted for manipulating dreams and instead use soulscapes like a hammer if resonance or Lair Traits are present. A Horror in a Bastion separate from the Beast has already accounted for it.<br /> <br /> The most pertinent questions as all this goes is &quot;Is a Bastion that is having Lair traits imposed or is otherwise interlapped with a Lair harder to manipulate for weird soul/dream metaphysical differential reasons or not?&quot;(I'd argue probably not, but I can see why someone might say otherwise) and &quot;Can Beasts develop soft dreamweaving abilities though kinship to Changelings?&quot;(I'd argue yeah, probably.)<br /> <br /> Dreams are a window into the soul, and visa versa, but there are reasons there are no standing rules for the Lost's ability to affect souls or for the Children's ability to affect dreams-they are different mediums, and the tools that each have are built to task and in accordance to each's nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-18-2023, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T20:31:16-07:00","id":1508819,"title":"","content":"Right\u2026but what about the Nightmares that wait until the next sleep? How do those work from the inside?<br /> <br /> Edit: Should I take this conversation to the Beast forum? I don\u2019t want to derail the thread with Beast metaphysics when it\u2019s only going to be a small part of the project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 04-18-2023, 11:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T20:39:03-07:00","id":1508820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508819#post1508819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right\u2026but what about the Nightmares that wait until the next sleep? How do those work from the inside?</div> </div> </div> </div>Admittedly a more interesting question I didn't account for. I'll have to wait till I can grab my copy of the BPG for a detailed answer, but off my head, though, that runs into a catch that Nightmares functionally plunge a soul/-equivalent* into the Primordial Dream. The dreams as they are in the Bastion (probably) don't much factor into it so much as the act of falling asleep is a good psychospiritual semiotic for what happens there.<br /> <br /> *Well, more the seat for the soul/-equivalent, given that souls aren't strictly the whole of a person's essence. Soulless people and monsters can be afflicted by Nightmares and all that jazz.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-18-2023, 11:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T20:53:47-07:00","id":1508823,"title":"","content":"Would like to point out that the way hobgoblins manage in the mortal world is largely that they don't \u2014 Kith and Kin points out that hobgoblins look at the Lost having a connection to the Wyrd and being attached to the land of the mundane as a baffling contradiction, and the corebook notes that hobgoblins belong in the Hedge and generally stay there, to the point where (barring Storyteller adjustment) they suffer the Deprived Condition and powerful specimens vanish back to the Hedge at sunrise/sunset; Oak Ash and Thorn similarly cites the general rarity of hobgoblins venturing into the mortal world as the reason most entitlement tokens that can be found out and about are in appropriate spots outside of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Hobgoblins operate normally or worse when removed from their native plane, which doesn't really feel like it needs general elaboration \u2014 if they're wandering the streets in the land of iron, something's gone wrong, but we have mechanics for how that works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T20:54:22-07:00","id":1508824,"title":"","content":"That said (posting as a second post to not trigger the spam filter), given that Nightmares tend to wake when they're triggered, Bastions probably don't really get much of a chance to form and reflect the Nightmare-though if you have an exceptional situation where the Nightmare both triggers AND the victim can't wake up, the Bastion probably abruptly changes channels towards the repetition of the Nightmare's premise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T20:56:42-07:00","id":1508826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508819#post1508819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right\u2026but what about the Nightmares that wait until the next sleep? How do those work from the inside?<br /> <br /> Edit: Should I take this conversation to the Beast forum? I don\u2019t want to derail the thread with Beast metaphysics when it\u2019s only going to be a small part of the project.</div> </div> </div> </div>Homebrew off the top of my head, away from my pdfs atm: Supernatural powers that warp or key off dreams/sleep (not just Begotten Nightmares) are visible in the Bastion as, mostly, circumstances and environments. If the changeling visited the victim\u2019s dreams before, she\u2019ll recognize that something\u2019s not quite right. From there, the changeling can use oneiromancy to neutralize the power. It\u2019s still there, just ineffectively so (like what happens with Awakened spells that are Withstood). If the original user of the power somehow loses control over the power, it becomes an Eidolon and wrecks havoc. Sometimes, such Eidolons slip outside the Dreaming Roads and into the wider Hedge, becoming Night Horror-worthy monsters that are uncannily familiar with supernaturals that \u2018birthed\u2019 them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T20:59:24-07:00","id":1508827,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this is going be a lot. I\u2019m taking it to the Beast side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T02:46:54-07:00","id":1508871,"title":"","content":"Could I perhaps add a new True Fae to this? The OP doesn't mention that the book includes sample True Fae, but it IS a Night Horrors fan-book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T07:01:02-07:00","id":1508882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508823#post1508823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would like to point out that the way hobgoblins manage in the mortal world is largely that they don't \u2014 Kith and Kin points out that hobgoblins look at the Lost having a connection to the Wyrd and being attached to the land of the mundane as a baffling contradiction, and the corebook notes that hobgoblins belong in the Hedge and generally stay there, to the point where (barring Storyteller adjustment) they suffer the Deprived Condition and powerful specimens vanish back to the Hedge at sunrise/sunset; Oak Ash and Thorn similarly cites the general rarity of hobgoblins venturing into the mortal world as the reason most entitlement tokens that can be found out and about are in appropriate spots outside of the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Hobgoblins operate normally or worse when removed from their native plane, which doesn't really feel like it needs general elaboration \u2014 if they're wandering the streets in the land of iron, something's gone wrong, but we have mechanics for how that works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I get page numbrers for this?<br /> <br /> Also I want Hobs to in ironside, I thought their would be some resources that one can not get in the hedge, Easier prey for eating, and again, could just be lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T07:19:32-07:00","id":1508884,"title":"","content":"If the overarching theme of the critters here is Pain, then a hobgoblin or three being stuck here, likely due to a bad bargain, while suffering the Deprived Condition (or worse) does make sense. Although they would still be rare misfortunates.<br /> <br /> Or maybe some of these hobgoblins aren\u2019t really at Ironside; what really happens is that there\u2019s an inconspicuous Hedgeway that leads to a part of the Hedge that\u2019s deceptively urban, looking like an abandoned bad part of the neighborhood, that has too many debris and junk sharp enough to cut jeans just outside the broad roads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T07:42:50-07:00","id":1508887,"title":"","content":"I think I'd like to contribute my WIP write-ups for two Leech Courts - which is, Courts whose Bargains are inherently flawed and detrimental, either to themselves or to those who share a Freehold with them.<br /> <br /> First is the <i>Sensory Courts</i> (exactly the five you're thinking of right now) whose Bargain makes them extremely hard to perceive by mortals, Lost and Fae alike. A way to explore the theme of disenchantment, the pain of silence and isolation... but also, potential betrayal: depending on which Court reigns, some senses of the local Gentry and their Huntsmen are dulled... but other sharpens.<br /> <br /> The other would be the three <i>Reckless Courts</i>: Truth, Dare or Shot, whose main strength is peer pressure. Their Bargain involves one Court pestering a Freehold with increasingly disturbing pranks ... and forcing the current Monarch to choose between two solutions offered by each of the remaining Courts. Truth or Dare ? <br /> <br /> I don't know whether I'll build a unitary set of rules for Leech Courts Mantle, but if anyone has interest in a similar concept, maybe that can make a chapter ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11431-adrasalieth","name":"Adrasalieth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T07:51:56-07:00","id":1508888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Adrasalieth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508887#post1508887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'd like to contribute my WIP write-ups for two Leech Courts - which is, Courts whose Bargains are inherently flawed and detrimental, either to themselves or to those who share a Freehold with them.<br /> <br /> First is the <i>Sensory Courts</i> (exactly the five you're thinking of right now) whose Bargain makes them extremely hard to perceive by mortals, Lost and Fae alike. A way to explore the theme of disenchantment, the pain of silence and isolation... but also, potential betrayal: depending on which Court reigns, some senses of the local Gentry and their Huntsmen are dulled... but other sharpens.<br /> <br /> The other would be the three <i>Reckless Courts</i>: Truth, Dare or Shot, whose main strength is peer pressure. Their Bargain involves one Court pestering a Freehold with increasingly disturbing pranks ... and forcing the current Monarch to choose between two solutions offered by each of the remaining Courts. Truth or Dare ?<br /> <br /> I don't know whether I'll build a unitary set of rules for Leech Courts Mantle, but if anyone has interest in a similar concept, maybe that can make a chapter ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good, you may add the chapter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T09:32:32-07:00","id":1508896,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27385_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27385\" data-vbnamecard=\"27385\">Cross-a-way</a> <br /> <br /> &quot;Mortals doubt a changeling\u2019s sanity when she insists that she travels to worlds beyond mundane ken. Likewise, her attachment to the mortal world baffles hobgoblins and the Gentry; to them, Wyrd marks the Lost as denizens of the Hedge and Arcadia, not humans. Mortals and faeries alike fail to acknowledge that changelings are creatures of both worlds.&quot; - Kith and Kin, page 26<br /> <br /> &quot;Hobgoblins belong in the Hedge, and generally stay there... A goblin in the mortal world suffers the Deprived Condition; goblins with Wyrd 6+ must bring a piece of the Hedge with them, and can only stay until the sun next crosses the horizon without other magic to keep them from vanishing back to the Hedge. The Storyteller may always dial these traits up or down according to the purpose a hobgoblin serves in the story.&quot; - Changeling the Lost 2e, page 253<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T09:50:27-07:00","id":1508898,"title":"","content":"Thank you <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27667_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27667\" data-vbnamecard=\"27667\">Super Vlad</a> <br /> <br /> Their are goblin markets in the Ironside so, having goblins wander around a bit ironside isnt too crazy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T15:10:22-07:00","id":1508931,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4443_5.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4443\" data-vbnamecard=\"4443\">GibberingEloquence</a> You may add a section on the true fea on the main doc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T18:01:07-07:00","id":1508956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1508882#post1508882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I get page numbrers for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to the ones Vlad already got, here's the bit from OA&amp;T:<br /> <br /> &quot;Goblins scour the Hedge for lost heraldry tokens to sell back to changelings, but rarely venture into the mundane world. Thus, the mundane world boasts more lost entitlements than the Hedge. These tokens gravitate to places that mirror their legends \u2014 the Queen of Hearts\u2019 scepter is always found in or near a rose garden, for instance.\u200b&quot; - Oak, Ash, &amp; Thorn, p32, &quot;Heraldry Tokens Out and About&quot; sidebar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also I want Hobs to in ironside, I thought their would be some resources that one can not get in the hedge, Easier prey for eating, and again, could just be lost. </div> </div> </div>Oh, you can totally have hobgoblins doing business outside the fae lands, but it should be thoroughly understood that hobgoblins are not changelings; pending The Hedge providing some indication to the contrary, they can't use portaling to create Hedgeways at will and are subject to the same limitations as humans are vis-a-vis needing Keys to open Hedgeways and not being guaranteed a return trip, and they suffer withdrawal symptoms no matter how full of Glamour they are.<br /> <br /> Hobs who regularly venture out of the Hedge do so from a Hollow or from Hedgeways they know the means and/or schedule of opening, which is where you get those nice motific patterns of behavior and spheres of activity from without needing to justify personlike actors from a parallel universe literally wandering the streets outside the context of being very lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T14:36:00-07:00","id":1509099,"title":"","content":"Wanted thoughts on initial drafts on Loyalist (specifically Privateer and True Loyalist) merits!<br /> Note: These are made for NPCs, so they might be a bit broken.<br /> <br /> <b>Fae Sanity (\u2022)</b><br /> <i>Prerequisite: Pledged to a True Fae</i><br /> Your character no longer suffers Clarity attacks from a certain type of action chosen by the True Fae. This could range from betrayal, murder, human contact, durance reminders, or dream manipulation, but never Seeming curses. This Merit is tied to a specific minor frailty the True Fae has, that your character then gains.<br /> <br /> <b>Power, Pleasure, Profit (\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <i>Prerequisite: Pledged to a True Fae</i><br /> Once per scene, when your character pursues an Aspiration of their True Fae, he regains a single Willpower point.<br /> <br /> <b>Faerie Favor (Loyalist) (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <i>Prerequisite: Pledged to a True Fae</i><br /> Instead of losing the merit upon calling in the favor, it goes into stasis. You can replenish the favor by:<ul><li>Completing your True Fae's Aspiration</li> <li>Strike a significant blow against the Lost</li> <li>Bringing someone to Arcadia</li> </ul>Notoriety doesn't apply to Loyalists, but if other changelings find out, you are instead marked for death.<br /> <br /> <b>Master's Hands (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b>\u200b<b>)</b><br /> <i>Prerequisite: Pledged to a True Fae</i><br /> Performing a Hedgespinning act that fits within the legend of the pledged True Fae's identity gains one automatic success. At three dots, gain two automatic successes. At five dots, gain three automatic successes.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T17:58:44-07:00","id":1509123,"title":"","content":"Very good, these will make wonderful addations<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-21T21:23:11-07:00","id":1509251,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27385_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27385\" data-vbnamecard=\"27385\">Cross-a-way</a> do you have an idea of what you want to see from Beast crossover? This is a Night Horror, so I\u2019m going to assume it\u2019s antagonistic, but like what\u2019s the framing? Just this is something/someone you can encounter? Or more like seeing their after effects of what they can do?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T10:20:43-07:00","id":1509298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1508759-night-horrors-scourging-thorns-an-fan-project?p=1509251#post1509251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27385_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27385\" data-vbnamecard=\"27385\">Cross-a-way</a> do you have an idea of what you want to see from Beast crossover? This is a Night Horror, so I\u2019m going to assume it\u2019s antagonistic, but like what\u2019s the framing? Just this is something/someone you can encounter? Or more like seeing their after effects of what they can do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly exploring the primordial dream, them dealing with some common beast Horrors, and what going into a beast's dream is like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T10:21:19-07:00","id":1509299,"title":"","content":"we aint their yet though, but if you wanna add something you can<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-04T06:57:25-07:00","id":1510701,"title":"","content":"Here's a Bridge-Burner style merit on dream-killing! Feedback and thoughts are welcome!<br /> \u200b<br /> <b>Death of Dreams (\u2022 to \u2022\u2022\u2022, Style)</b><ul><li><b>Weaken Dream (\u2022):</b> When your character is inside a Bastion she may spend a Willpower point to lower its Fortification rating by -2 for one turn, which affects the traits of all the important eidolons within as normal. This cannot stack with others using this same technique.</li> <li><b>Dream Monster (\u2022\u2022):</b> Your character may reflexively spend a point of Glamour to act as an Eidolon or Oneiropomp she can see\u2019s minor bane frailty until the beginning of her next turn.</li> <li><b>Raze Dream (\u2022\u2022\u2022):</b> A terrifying technique that mutilates a dream beyond comprehension. When resolving the Dream Assailant Condition through destroying an important Eidolon or prop, she may inflict Ravaged Condition <i>permanently</i>. This ruins all further dreams the dreamer has, making their Bastion a ruined husk of what it once was. This can be cured through a paradigm shift costing 8 successes.\u200b</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Bargains\" target=\"_blank\">Curiouser and Curiouser Bargains</a></b>, a collection of 30+ Homebrew Contracts and 10+ Entitlements on the STV!<br /> My <b><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1GFE19F9st7dhGh9zv_hEQyOSm80Xp7dQwmvFg2SAXJY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules</a></b> for Changeling!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/17SsOsKpfdANVZscFHSO_afTx-gD3h0iX3p5q07V4u50/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Vampire!<br /> My <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1kR6ASTLjaEDwl3zgANnkRrbk0-s2bvw40uXwS-q15O0/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><b>House Rules</b></a> for Geist!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27667-super-vlad","name":"Super Vlad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27667_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-07T10:20:39-07:00","id":1510992,"title":"","content":"Added, as per some people's request, a section on Huntsman! There are currently two example ones in the document right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Proud creator of <b><a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/420206/Curiouser-and-Curiouser-Barg